                        <a name="mrm1">What is tribal mrm?</a><!--End-->
                        <h1>Tribal MRM</h1>
                        <p>Relative to Customer Relationship Management(CRM). The Avatar Growers platform has established Member Relationship Management(MRM)</p>
                        <p>The personalization of MRM and benefits &Aacute; Features that members cannot find anywhere else is what sets us apart.</p>
                        <!-- ####################################################################################################### -->
                        <a name="mrm2">How do I set up my mrm account?</a><!--End-->
                        <h1>Tribal Account</h1>
                        <p>Your account is automatically set-up from the creation of your card. To successfully unlock all the benefits of the program members only need to follow the goals set forth on their member dash.</p>
                        <div class="img-responsive">
                            <div class="row">
                                <p class="imgholder"><span><img src="~/KnowledgeShots/memdash1.png" width="200" height="100" alt="picture" /></span></p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <!-- ####################################################################################################### -->
                        <a name="mrm3">What are the benefits of the mrm account?</a><!--End-->
                        <h1>Account Benefits</h1>
                        <p>By following the goals set forth on your induvidual member dash you can track, measure, increase the benefits that are available to every member.</p>
                        <p>The more members follow their goal-set as a active member or benefiting member more options are available and increased benefits will appear on your dash.</p>
                        <div class="img-responsive">
                            <div class="row">
                                <p class="imgholder"><span><img src="~/KnowledgeShots/memdash2.png" width="200" height="100" alt="picture" /></span></p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <!-- ####################################################################################################### -->
                        <a name="card1">What is the tribal card?</a><!--End-->
                        <h1>Tribal Card</h1>
                        <p>Our member cards are similar to and can be used like any traditional debit/credit card.</p>
                        <p>Tribal cards have additional features for our members. Please review your card service contract for a complete list of card features.</p>
                        <!-- ####################################################################################################### -->
                        <a name="card2">Why should I use my tribal card?</a><!--End-->
                        <h1>Payment Card</h1>
                        <p>While consumers are able to use any payment method they choose, we suggest our members use their member card for all member activities and purchases.</p>
                        <!-- ####################################################################################################### -->
                        <a name="card3">What if I loose my tribal card?</a><!--End-->
                        <h1>Lost Card</h1>
                        <p>Card loss can happen to anyone. Any current member can call a representative to have cards cancelled or renewed.</p>
